# Normalise line endings to LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true) rewrites text
# files with CRLF, which changes their *raw bytes*. Two things in this
# repo hash or byte-compare raw bytes and would then diverge from the
# Linux baseline that the goldens were generated on:
#
#   * tests/test_netgraph_golden.py SHA-256s circuit.schema.json to
#     derive `schema_version` — CRLF flips the digest and fails the
#     golden on Windows only (the update script can't fix it: on Linux
#     the hash already matches, so --bump-schema-version is refused).
#   * scripts/check_gallery_regression.py byte-compares committed SVGs
#     against freshly-rendered output, and the renderer always emits
#     "\n".
#
# Forcing eol=lf keeps the bytes identical across Linux and Windows CI.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated schematics are byte-compared by the gallery regression gate;
# pin them to LF explicitly so a Windows checkout matches renderer output.
*.svg text eol=lf

# Binary types git must never convert (belt-and-suspenders over the
# text=auto auto-detection above).
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.ico  binary
